t for the watchdog's post-`docker start` check (reuse MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT) so it cannot hold the deploy flock unbounded on a crash-looping backend.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.265,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["autodeploy.sh:1050-1052 bounds the bot readiness loop with HEALTH_TIMEOUT/deadline; mcp uses MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT (mcp-entrypoint.sh:14)","The flock is held across the up-to-date no-op path (autodeploy.sh:780 acquire, 818-824 no-op), so a synchronous readiness wait blocks every other component's tick","ABSENCE: plan specifies readiness-checks the port but names no timeout/deadline for the watchdog's wait"],"finding":"The watchdog's readiness check runs synchronously inside the deploy flock on the up-to-date/no-op tick, but the plan does not name a bounded readiness timeout for it, unlike the existing bot (HEALTH_TIMEOUT) and blue-green (MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT) paths.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc40ac7f7e4365d88","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA / design decision — 'runs `docker start <live-container>` and readiness-checks that same port'","norm_id":"ndfa9dcef6da344b7","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Live container starts but never becomes ready (crash-looping app); the watchdog's readiness loop spins","Concurrent review-bot deploy waits on the flock while the watchdog blocks"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the watchdog readiness-checks the live port with the existing MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT deadline, and on timeout treats it as a failed start (emit mcp-live-backend-down, record mcp backoff, retry next tick) rather than looping.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition of the self-heal failure arm explicitly: is docker-start/readiness failure always treated as retryable/transient (backoff + retry), and if so, how does an operator distinguish a permanently-unstartable backend from a transient crash so it is escalated rather than retried indefinitely?","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.801,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'failure leaves the container/upstream identity intact, emits existing AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-live-backend-down, records MCP backoff, and retries later'","No explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) is attached to the docker-start/readiness failure arm; the plan asserts unbounded retry-later without distinguishing a transient crash from a permanent start failure."],"finding":"The self-heal failure arm (docker start or readiness fails) is described only as 'records MCP backoff, and retries later', but the plan never states its disposition explicitly (transient/retryable vs fatal/permanent). A permanently-unstartable container (missing image, corrupt config) would be treated identically to a transient crash and retried indefinitely, with the operator's only signal being the repeated AUTODEPLOY_ERROR.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffbab0f258a521fc8","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA / design decision — 'failure leaves the container/upstream identity intact, emits ... AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-live-backend-down, records MCP backoff, and retries later'","norm_id":"nb60b6d0c539146d2","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A live MCP container that cannot start (image pulled away / bad config) triggers the watchdog every tick, records backoff, and emits AUTODEPLOY_ERROR forever — the 502 persists and the retry loop masks that this is a fatal condition needing human intervention."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a one-line failure-disposition statement: e.g. 'a failed start/readiness stays retryable (backoff + retry-later); AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-live-backend-down is the operator escalation signal, and repeated occurrences past N backoff cycles indicate a fatal condition requiring manual intervention.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"non